-# What a cascading delete withdraws, before the reason and the typed title.
-#
-# Locals:
-#   cascade — the container's TombstoneTargets
-#   kind    — "collection" or "community"
-#   title   — the container's title, plain text
- parts = cascade.counts.reject { |_type, count| count.zero? }.map { |type, count| pluralize(count, type.downcase) }
%p
  This withdraws
  %strong= title
  and everything live inside it:
  = "#{parts.to_sentence}."
- if cascade.over_limit?
  .alert.alert-warning.py-2.px-3.small.d-flex.align-items-start.mb-0
    %i.fa-solid.fa-triangle-exclamation.me-2.mt-1{'aria-hidden' => 'true'}
    %span
      That is more than #{number_with_delimiter(TombstoneTargets::LIMIT)} items, so it can't be deleted from here. Ask the development team to delete this #{kind}.
- else
  .alert.alert-warning.py-2.px-3.small.d-flex.align-items-start
    %i.fa-solid.fa-triangle-exclamation.me-2.mt-1{'aria-hidden' => 'true'}
    %span
      There is no one-step restore. Each item can be restored on its own from the tombstone registry, parents first. To bring everything back, ask the development team: Requests &amp; activity will list every item withdrawn.
